item.description:
The concordance model, with most observations 'agree' on this matter. Have raised two extra component of <a data-href="Background matter scaling" href="cosmology-notes/background-matter-scaling.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Background matter scaling</a> beyond the Standard Model.Sometimes called The Standard Model of Cosmology.The Ingredients are:
<br><a data-href="Photons" href="cosmology-notes/photons.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Photons</a>, radiation;
<br><a data-href="Neutrino" href="cosmology-notes/neutrino.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Neutrino</a>s;
<br><a data-href="Baryons" href="cosmology-notes/baryons.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Baryons</a> from <a data-href="Big-bang Nucleosynthesis" href="cosmology-notes/big-bang-nucleosynthesis.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Big-bang Nucleosynthesis</a>
<br><a data-href="Dark Matter" href="cosmology-notes/dark-matter.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Dark Matter</a>;
<br><a data-href="Dark Energy" href="cosmology-notes/dark-energy.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Dark Energy</a>.<br>
See <a data-href="Background matter scaling" href="cosmology-notes/background-matter-scaling.html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Background matter scaling</a>.
The contribution of radiation and baryons by stars
The contribution to from stars only.<br>
The contribution to from glowing matter . This means that most baryons are in the form of cold, warm and hot gases, usually in the <a data-href="Intergalactic Medium (IGM)" href=".html" class="internal-link" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Intergalactic Medium (IGM)</a>.
